// 'Country Kitchen' — Jay-Artist (CC BY 3.0; original at
// blendswap.com/blends/view/42851). A sunlit farmhouse kitchen — the
// window plane carries the main area light, three downlights fill the
// counter. Official pbrt-v4 export from
// https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/ — `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh
// kitchen` materializes the source; this RON was bootstrapped once by
// `cenote-cli import sources/bitterli/kitchen/scene-v4.pbrt` and is
// the source of truth — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it.
// Native oracle: pbrt path, maxdepth 17.
//
// Import fidelity: two knowing gaps that fully account for the
// divergence. The window Blinds are a diffuse-transmission material
// with no OpenPBR lobe — imported as opaque diffuse, the transmittance
// dropped — so the rolled blind above the window reads matte instead
// of sun-backlit (unlock: a diffuse-transmission lobe, material-depth
// work, unassigned). And the Cushion1/BreadBinFront displacement
// textures are ignored (same bucket) — the bread bin loses its
// embossed lettering, the cushions their weave shading. Degrade the
// pbrt reference the same two ways and the eighth-res RMSE falls from
// 0.053 to 0.015, the gap-free baseline — nothing else diverges. The
// ×39 anisotropic-roughness warnings are all equal-axis — averaging is
// exact, not a gap; texture `filter` hints are cosmetic.
